1606		Put $n=2m+2$. The directly indexed extended line-point law samples
1607		$i\in\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ and $u,v\in\F_q^n$ independently and uniformly,
1608		and chooses the axis or diagonal kind with equal probabilities.
1609		For the axis kind set $w=e_i$; for the diagonal kind set $w_j=0$ for
1610		$j<i$ and $w_j=v_j$ for $j\ge i$. The line has base $L_w^{\mathrm{lnf}}(u)$
1611		and direction $w$, retaining its kind and coordinate index; the sampled
1612		point is $u$. Zero diagonal directions are included.
