1614		A directly indexed sub-line law $D_{\mathrm{dir}}$ is a probability law
1615		on triples $(\ell,\ell_X,\ell_Z)$ with the following properties.
1616		Its extended-line marginal is the line marginal just defined.
1617		Every supported triple admits affine maps $t\mapsto a_W+b_Wt$ such that
1618		\[
1619			\pi_W(\ell(t))=\ell_W(a_W+b_Wt),\qquad W\in\{X,Z\},
